course: dictionary
lesson: 12221
title: Words that show choice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell us how someone does something. «Consciously» is one of them. It means you know what you are doing and you do it on purpose. «She consciously chose to be kind» tells us she thought about it first.
explain: Look at the words around it. Words like decide, choose or pick often sit nearby, so they are the clues that a thought came before the action. Test your meaning by swapping it in: «She chose to be kind on purpose» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: The word has a second meaning too: being aware of something while it happens. «I wasn't consciously listening» means you were not really paying attention, even though you could hear. Breathing is different. You do it automatically, without deciding, so it is not something you do consciously.
fact: Consciously is an adverb, made from the word conscious.
fact: «Consciously» means on purpose and knowing what you are doing: «She consciously chose to be kind».
fact: «Consciously» can also mean while being aware of something: «I wasn't consciously listening».
fact: Things you do automatically, like breathing and blinking, happen without you deciding them.
fact: In stories, «consciously» often shows a character's choice.
exercise: «He consciously decided to tell the truth.» What does consciously mean here? | Very quickly | While he was asleep | By accident, without thinking | *On purpose, knowing what he was doing
exercise: Which action is usually done automatically, not consciously? | *Blinking | Deciding what to eat | Choosing your words | Picking a colour
exercise: «She consciously chose the red pen.» Find and copy the word that shows a choice was made. | red | *chose | the | pen
test: «I wasn't consciously listening, so I missed the bell.» What does the sentence tell us? | He could not hear anything at all | *He was not really paying attention | He listened very carefully on purpose | He was asleep and dreaming
test: «Mia consciously picked the quietest seat.» Why did she pick it? | It was the only seat left | She sat there by accident | She was too sleepy to look for another seat | *She thought about it and chose it on purpose
exam: «Ravi consciously decided to forgive his brother.» What is the best meaning of consciously here? | He was too tired to talk | He forgave by accident | He forgot what his brother had done | *He chose to forgive on purpose
